event: response.reasoning_summary_text.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","item_id":"rs_044b98d1688e9f84016aca901551848194a21bb7590015bfbf","output_index":0,"sequence_number":115,"summary_index":0,"text":"**Implementing SSR Forms**\n\nI need to implement simple server-side rendering (SSR) for forms with HTTP redirects and native labels, avoiding dependencies. I want to ensure SSR meets tests, possibly with a button to navigate and create a DOM page without requiring JavaScript. It seems unnecessary to add client scripts since SSR should work effectively on its own. The application should handle forms with POST actions and open GET requests using action, while managing SQLite ID integers for persistence and error handling. I'll also consider conducting built-in integration tests for my temporary server restart. I've got enough time to finalize this!"}

event: response.reasoning_summary_part.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_part.done","item_id":"rs_044b98d1688e9f84016aca901551848194a21bb7590015bfbf","output_index":0,"part":{"type":"summary_text","text":"**Implementing SSR Forms**\n\nI need to implement simple server-side rendering (SSR) for forms with HTTP redirects and native labels, avoiding dependencies. I want to ensure SSR meets tests, possibly with a button to navigate and create a DOM page without requiring JavaScript. It seems unnecessary to add client scripts since SSR should work effectively on its own. The application should handle forms with POST actions and open GET requests using action, while managing SQLite ID integers for persistence and error handling. I'll also consider conducting built-in integration tests for my temporary server restart. I've got enough time to finalize this!"},"sequence_number":116,"summary_index":0}

